-- A definition with no GIVEN of its own, right after clauses of the same name,
-- with another number of inputs than they have patterns, is not another clause.
-- It is a rule of its own whose inputs are called Red and Blue, so f Green Red
-- gives 3 (found by the pre-review of legalese/l4-ide#545, 2026-10-13). The
-- warning says so, at the definition. A definition with a GIVEN of its own is
-- that rule written out, and draws none.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE f Red IS 1
DECIDE f c IS 2
DECIDE f Red Blue IS 3

GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE g Red IS 1
DECIDE g c IS 2

GIVEN c IS A Colour
      d IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
g c d MEANS 3

#EVAL f Red
#EVAL f Green
#EVAL f Green Red
#EVAL g Green Red
